#. type: Content of: <div><h1>
#: index.html:6
msgid "What is Supplemental Linux From Scratch?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: index.html:9
msgid ""
"Supplemental Linux From Scratch aims to supplement an LFS installation and "
"supports LFS, MLFS, BLFS, and GLFS. In essence, SLFS is a sort of BLFS 2, "
"but doesn't include any of the pages from BLFS, except for some cases where "
"a package needs to be re-installed for compatibility."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: index.html:16
msgid ""
"The focus of SLFS is generalized and contains a wide array of packages to "
"install from, such as general monitoring utilities like htop or BTOP++ or "
"fetch programs like fastfetch, to video game emulators like Dolphin or "
"Mupen64Plus, graphical environments like Hyprland and CDE, multimedia "
"libraries that enhance existing packages in BLFS (FFmpeg and MLT) like "
"Rubberband and LADSPA-SDK, and support for binaries and containers like "
"Fuse2 and Flatpak. This list isn't exaughstive."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: index.html:26
msgid ""
"As the focus of SLFS is similar to BLFS, it also exists to offload any "
"potential BLFS package additions to reduce burden on maintainers of BLFS."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: index.html:31
msgid ""
"Since BLFS provides such a large base of packages, SLFS externally links to "
"a given page if a package calls for a dependency in BLFS. At other times, "
"the links will point to within the book or GLFS."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h2>
#: index.html:37
msgid "Why would I want a SLFS system?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: index.html:40
msgid ""
"BLFS provides a lot of packages that can get users to either 100% of 80% of "
"what they need from a system. The problem is the remaining percentage of "
"packages that may have complicated installation instructions or just takes "
"too long to do manually. SLFS helps bridge the gap and gets users closer to "
"that 100%."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h2>
#: index.html:48
msgid "What can I do with my SLFS system?"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: index.html:51
msgid ""
"You will be able to use various system monitoring utilites, fetch programs, "
"a YouTube video downloading tool, SDL3, various terminal emulators, "
"application launchers, screenshot tools, wallpapers selectors, OBS-Studio, "
"IMEs, various graphical environments like Hyprland, CDE, and Wayfire, "
"various computer and video game emulators, a Minecraft launcher, SVR4-style "
"tooling, Flatpak, and enable libvpl and Intel-MediaSDK support in various "
"packages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><h2>
#: index.html:60
msgid "Read Online"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <div><p>
#: index.html:63
msgid ""
"You can read the book <a href=\"https://glfs-book.github.io/slfs\">here.</a> "
"The book is rolling release, like MLFS and GLFS. The only online rendered "
"version right now is System V, although you can <a href=\"/slfs/download."
"html\">download</a> the edition of the book that has Systemd support."
msgstr ""

